<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Asturica Augusta</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Asturica Augusta was the Roman town on the site of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/astorga">Astorga</a> in north-western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a>, founded after Augustus' <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cantabrian-wars">Cantabrian Wars</a> in the land of the Astures. It became the administrative centre of the gold-mining district that included <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/las-medulas">Las Médulas</a> and an important road junction. It later belonged to the province of Gallaecia.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/asturica-augusta.jpg" alt="Asturica Augusta" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Rodelar · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Detalle_Asturica.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
